    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d610">

                <pb facs="0880" n="870" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg870"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P.W./5–1545</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-05-15">May 15, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Following a meeting on May 12
                    between the Secretary of Navy, Mr. McCloy,<anchor n="32" xml:id="d610-f1"/> and
                    Ambassador Harriman to consider political implications of the expected Soviet
                    entry in the Far Eastern war, the attached memorandum<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d610-f2"/> at the request of the War and Navy Departments was sent
                    by me to Secretaries Stimson and Forrestal. We are awaiting their replies before
                    holding another meeting with Ambassador Harriman prior to his return to Moscow.
                    I will, of course, keep you informed of any further developments on this
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I understand that you discussed this general matter with Ambassador Harriman
                    before he left San Francisco.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
